Gemini's D1 (ZWNJ fix survives 10 joins) was reproduced and confirmed;
its own test is now the permanent regression test, strengthened to assert
the ZWNJ count after every individual join rather than only the final
result.

Gemini's D2 conclusion ("the r/f collision is a unique artifact") was
checked directly and found false, exactly as a follow-up critique
document argued: built the exact collision matrix it specified and
confirmed a bare consonant before an independent vowel collides with
that consonant + a dependent vowel-matra for every vowel class, not only
vocalic r/rr. This is now a permanent test
(SLP1BareConsonantVowelCollision).

Went one step further than the critique document's own next step,
rather than assuming a transliteration-level collision must be an engine
bug: checked whether letting every other vowel class fall through to the
default (dependent-matra) rendering ever produces wrong output. It
doesn't, for the only real (not synthetic) examples available: RV
1.1.2's attested Samhita-patha shows "r+ii" -> dependent matra and
"r+u" -> dependent matra (both verified by direct Unicode codepoint
inspection), matching this engine's existing default. No speculative
widening of _finish_consonant_then_vowel was made without a reproduced
defect. Both its docstring and the module docstring were corrected to
state the real reason for its scope (a Devanagari typesetting convention
specific to vocalic r/rr, confirmed by 3 attested data points) instead of
the disproven "uniquely ambiguous at the SLP1 level" framing.

Also flagged that the critique document's blanket rejection of Gemini's
Pāṇini 8.3.17/8.3.19 citation (for RV 1.1.7's still-open visarga gap) was
procedurally correct for that prompt's own rule but too quick to discard
substantively -- it's a real sutra, and "Śākalya" is this recension's own
namesake -- recorded as an open lead to verify, not adopted or dismissed.

Architecture doc sec.6.9 and PENDING.md record the full verification
trail.

